(   The Three Mutual Exclusive States:) Tj
T*
(   1. Pending: Initial state; operation is actively underway. Has neither resolved nor rejected.) Tj
T*
(   2. Fulfilled \(Resolved\): Operation completed successfully; holds a permanent resulting `value`.) Tj
T*
(   3. Rejected: Operation failed; holds an associated `reason` \(typically an Error object\).) Tj
T*
(   Once a Promise transitions from Pending to either Fulfilled or Rejected, it is 'Settled' and) Tj
T*
(   permanently locked \(immutable\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Promise Chaining Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   - Every `.then\(\)` or `.catch\(\)` call returns a BRAND NEW Promise.) Tj
T*
(   - If a callback returns a value, the new Promise resolves with that value.) Tj
T*
(   - If a callback returns another Promise, the new Promise adopts the state and value of that) Tj
T*
(   returned Promise.) Tj
T*
(   - If a callback throws an exception, the returned Promise immediately transitions to Rejected.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Compare Promise concurrency methods: Promise.all\(\), Promise.allSettled\(\), Promise.race\(\), and Promise.any\(\) with engineering use cases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   ES6 and subsequent specifications provide four distinct concurrency combinators for) Tj
T*
(   coordinating multiple asynchronous operations:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. `Promise.all\([p1, p2, p3]\)` \(All-or-Nothing\):) Tj
T*
(   - Resolves when ALL promises fulfill; rejects IMMEDIATELY if any single promise rejects.) Tj
T*
(   - Use Case: Loading dashboard widgets where all datasets are mandatory before rendering.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. `Promise.allSettled\([p1, p2, p3]\)` \(Tolerant Batching\):) Tj
T*
(   - Waits for all promises to settle \(either fulfill or reject\), returning an array of descriptor) Tj
T*
(   objects `{ status, value/reason }`.) Tj
T*
(   - Use Case: Bulk email dispatch where failure of one email should not halt the remaining) Tj
T*
(   dispatches.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. `Promise.race\([p1, p2, p3]\)` \(Fastest Settler\):) Tj
T*
(   - Settles as soon as the first promise settles \(fulfills OR rejects\).) Tj
T*
(   - Use Case: Implementing network request timeouts \(`Promise.race\([fetch\(url\),) Tj
T*
(   timeoutPromise]\)`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. `Promise.any\([p1, p2, p3]\)` \(Fastest Success\):) Tj
T*
(   - Fulfills as soon as the FIRST promise fulfills successfully; only rejects \(with) Tj
T*
(   AggregateError\) if EVERY single promise fails.) Tj
T*
(   - Use Case: Querying redundant CDN mirrors for an image asset.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
