/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Same-Origin Policy \(SOP\) and Cross-Origin Resource Sharing \(CORS\) protocol, detailing Simple Requests and Preflights.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Same-Origin Policy \(SOP\) is a foundational browser security model that restricts) Tj
T*
(   client-side scripts from reading responses originating from a different Origin \(defined by) Tj
T*
(   Scheme + Host + Port\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Cross-Origin Resource Sharing \(CORS\):) Tj
T*
(   CORS is a W3C standard allowing servers to selectively relax SOP via HTTP response headers) Tj
T*
(   \(`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://app.example.com`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Simple vs Preflighted Requests:) Tj
T*
(   1. Simple Requests:) Tj
T*
(   - Allowed methods: GET, HEAD, POST.) Tj
T*
(   - Permitted Content-Type: `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`, `multipart/form-data`,) Tj
T*
(   `text/plain`.) Tj
T*
(   - Dispatched directly without preliminary checks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Preflighted Requests \(OPTIONS\):) Tj
T*
(   - Triggered if request uses PUT, DELETE, PATCH, custom headers \(`Authorization`\), or) Tj
T*
(   `Content-Type: application/json`.) Tj
T*
(   - The browser automatically dispatches an preliminary HTTP `OPTIONS` request with) Tj
T*
(   `Access-Control-Request-Method` and `Access-Control-Request-Headers`.) Tj
T*
(   - The browser inspects the server's preflight response; if approved, it fires the actual) Tj
T*
ET

