/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the WebSocket protocol and API architecture, contrasting it with HTTP Polling, Long-Polling, and Server-Sent Events \(SSE\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Modern real-time applications require instant bidirectional communication between client and) Tj
T*
(   server:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Paradigm Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   1. Short Polling: Client sends repeated HTTP requests on a timer \(e.g. every 2 seconds\). High) Tj
T*
(   overhead: thousands of wasted HTTP headers.) Tj
T*
(   2. Long-Polling: Server holds request open until new data arrives, sends response, and client) Tj
T*
(   reconnects. Better latency, but high connection churn.) Tj
T*
(   3. Server-Sent Events \(SSE\): Unidirectional streaming \(Server -> Client\) over standard HTTP.) Tj
T*
(   Perfect for live stock tickers, but cannot send client data back.) Tj
T*
(   4. WebSockets \(ws:// and wss://\):) Tj
T*
(   - Full-Duplex Bidirectional Channel over a single persistent TCP connection.) Tj
T*
(   - Initiated via an HTTP Upgrade handshake, then switches to minimal 2-byte framing overhead.) Tj
T*
(   - Sub-millisecond latency ideal for multiplayer games, collaborative editors, and chat apps.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
