/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the architecture of the jQuery library, explaining the jQuery Object wrapper, DOM selection, and method chaining.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   jQuery revolutionized web development by abstracting browser discrepancies into a uniform,) Tj
T*
(   cross-browser API:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Core Architectural Principles:) Tj
T*
(   1. The jQuery Object Wrapper \(`$\(\)`\):) Tj
T*
(   - Calling `$\('div'\)` does not return raw DOM nodes; it returns a synthetic jQuery wrapper) Tj
T*
(   object containing matching nodes with wrapped helper methods.) Tj
T*
(   - Accessing raw node: `$\('div'\)[0]` or `$\('div'\).get\(0\)`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Method Chaining:) Tj
T*
(   - Almost all jQuery mutation methods return the calling jQuery object \(`return this;`\).) Tj
T*
(   - Allows chaining multiple animations, attribute modifications, and styling calls sequentially) Tj
T*
(   without re-querying the DOM:) Tj
T*
(   `$\('#alertBox'\).addClass\('highlight'\).slideDown\(400\).delay\(2000\).fadeOut\(400\);`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Implicit Iteration:) Tj
T*
(   - Methods automatically execute across ALL matching elements in the set without writing) Tj
T*
(   explicit loops \(e.g., `$\('p'\).css\('color', 'blue'\);` colors every paragraph\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
