(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Request Cancellation using AbortController with the Fetch API, demonstrating timeout implementations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike XMLHttpRequest which had an `abort\(\)` method, the Fetch API delegates cancellation to) Tj
T*
(   the standardized `AbortController` interface:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Implementing an Auto-Timeout Fetch Wrapper:) Tj
T*
(   ```javascript) Tj
T*
(   async function fetchWithTimeout\(url, options = {}, timeoutMs = 5000\) {) Tj
T*
