(   Core Response Headers:) Tj
T*
(   1. `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://client.example.com` - Explicitly permits origin) Tj
T*
(   \(wildcard `*` allows all, but disallows credentials\).) Tj
T*
(   2. `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` - Informs browser that cross-origin cookies or) Tj
T*
(   authorization headers can be exposed to frontend scripts.) Tj
T*
(   3. `Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS` - Lists acceptable HTTP) Tj
T*
(   verbs.) Tj
T*
(   4. `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, Authorization, X-Requested-With` - Whitelists) Tj
T*
(   custom request headers.) Tj
T*
(   5. `Access-Control-Max-Age: 86400` - Caches preflight OPTIONS verification for 24 hours \(86,400) Tj
T*
(   seconds\), eliminating redundant preflight roundtrips.) Tj
T*
(   6. `Access-Control-Expose-Headers: X-Custom-Header` - Whitelists custom response headers that) Tj
T*
(   frontend scripts are permitted to read via `response.headers.get\(\)`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
