(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Beacon API \(`navigator.sendBeacon\(\)`\) and contrast it with Fetch on page unload.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Transmitting telemetry data \(analytics, metrics\) when a user closes a browser tab was) Tj
T*
(   historically problematic:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Problem with Fetch/XHR on Unload:) Tj
T*
(   When an `unload` or `beforeunload` event fires, standard asynchronous `fetch\(\)` requests are) Tj
T*
(   often aborted immediately by the browser before headers transmit. Using synchronous XHR froze) Tj
T*
(   page closing, frustrating users.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Beacon API Solution:) Tj
T*
(   `navigator.sendBeacon\('/api/analytics', JSON.stringify\(metrics\)\);`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Operational Advantages:) Tj
T*
(   - Asynchronous & Non-Blocking: Does not delay page teardown.) Tj
T*
(   - Browser-Managed Delivery: The browser guarantees transmission in the background even after) Tj
T*
(   the tab or process has terminated.) Tj
T*
(   - Uses HTTP POST automatically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 30:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Network Waterfall diagnostics in Browser Developer Tools: Queuing, DNS Lookup, Initial Connection, TTFB, and Content Download.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Profiling asynchronous web requests requires mastering the Network panel waterfall timing) Tj
T*
(   diagram:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Waterfall Phases Breakdown:) Tj
T*
(   1. Queued / Stalled: Request was held in browser queue \(browsers cap simultaneous HTTP/1.1) Tj
T*
(   connections at 6 per domain\).) Tj
T*
(   2. DNS Lookup: Time spent resolving domain name to IP.) Tj
T*
(   3. Initial Connection \(TCP Handshake\): Time elapsed establishing TCP connection \(1 RTT\).) Tj
T*
(   4. SSL/TLS Negotiation: Time elapsed completing cryptographic TLS handshake.) Tj
T*
(   5. Request Sent: Time taken to push request bytes out across network interface.) Tj
T*
(   6. Time to First Byte \(TTFB\): Time waiting for server to process request and return first byte) Tj
T*
(   of response. High TTFB indicates slow backend server logic or database query bottlenecks.) Tj
T*
(   7. Content Download: Time taken to download the full response body payload. High download time) Tj
T*
(   indicates uncompressed assets or constrained bandwidth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
